'''''Kid Icarus: Of Myths and Monsters''''' is a 1991 [[Action game|action]]-[[Platformer|platform game]] developed and published by [[Nintendo]] for the [[Game Boy]]. It is a sequel to ''[[Kid Icarus]]'' (1986) for the [[Nintendo Entertainment System]]. It was released in North America on November 1991, and in Europe on May 21, 1992, but not in Japan where it was already developed until on February 8, 2012 through the [[Nintendo 3DS|3DS]] [[Virtual Console]]; this project retained its original English localization and commemorated the release of the following month's ''[[Kid Icarus: Uprising]]'' in the same region, followed by its re-release in Europe on March 8, and North America on July 19.<ref name="NLife">{{cite web |url=http://www.nintendolife.com/reviews/eshop/kid_icarus_of_myths_and_monsters_gameboy |title=Kid Icarus: Of Myths and Monsters |date=March 9, 2012 |publisher=NintendoLife |accessdate=March 9, 2012 |archive-date=March 11, 2012 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120311043925/http://www.nintendolife.com/reviews/eshop/kid_icarus_of_myths_and_monsters_gameboy |url-status=live}}</ref> The game was also re-released on the [[Nintendo Classics]] service on November 26, 2025.<ref name="11-26-2025">{{cite web | last=Romano | first=Sal | title=NES and Game Boy – Nintendo Classics add Battletoads, Ninja Gaiden II: The Dark Sword of Chaos, Bionic Commando, and Kid Icarus: Of Myths and Monsters | website=Gematsu | date=November 26, 2025 | url=https://www.gematsu.com/2025/11/nes-and-game-boy-nintendo-classics-add-battletoads-ninja-gaiden-ii-the-dark-sword-of-chaos-bionic-commando-and-kid-icarus-of-myths-and-monsters | access-date=November 26, 2025}}</ref> The story of ''Of Myths and Monsters'' is influenced by [[Greek mythology|Greek]] and [[Roman mythology]], and follows the angel soldier [[Pit (Kid Icarus)|Pit]] on his quest for three sacred treasures. His objective is to defeat the demon [[Orcus|Orcos]], who has invaded the kingdom of Angel Land. The game features the core gameplay mechanics of its predecessor. Players explore [[2D computer graphics|two-dimensional]] environments while collecting items and fighting monsters. ''Of Myths and Monsters'' was named the 18th best Game Boy game by ''[[Nintendo Power]]'', and commended by critics for its gameplay, graphics, and music.

