'''''Resident Evil'''''{{efn|Known in Japan as {{nihongo|'''''Bio Hazard'''''|バイオ ハザード|Baio Hazādo|lead=yes}}. The original game spelled the title as two words, instead of the one-word convention used from ''Biohazard 2'' and onward.}} is a 1996 [[survival horror]] video game developed and published by [[Capcom]] for the [[PlayStation (console)|PlayStation]]. It is the first main installment in Capcom's ''[[Resident Evil]]'' series. Set in the fictional Arklay mountain region in the [[Midwestern United States|Midwest]], players control [[Chris Redfield]] and [[Jill Valentine]], members of the elite task force [[List of Resident Evil characters|S.T.A.R.S.]], who must escape a [[Spencer Mansion|mansion]] infested with [[Zombies in Resident Evil|zombie]]s and other monsters.

''Resident Evil'' was conceived by the producer [[Tokuro Fujiwara]], inspired by the limitations on his 1989 horror game ''[[Sweet Home (video game)|Sweet Home]]''. It was directed by [[Shinji Mikami]]. It went through several redesigns, first as a [[Super Nintendo Entertainment System|Super NES]] game in 1993, then a fully 3D [[First-person (video games)|first-person]] PlayStation game in 1994 and finally a [[Third-person (video games)|third-person game]]. Gameplay consists of action, exploration, puzzle solving and inventory management. ''Resident Evil'' established many conventions seen later in the series, and in other survival horror games, including the inventory system, save system, and use of a vitals-monitoring system instead of a health counter.

''Resident Evil'' was praised for its graphics, gameplay, sound, and atmosphere, although it received criticism for its weak dialogue and voice acting. It was an international best-seller, and became the [[List of best-selling PlayStation video games|highest-selling PlayStation game]] at the time. By December 1997, it had sold about 4 million copies worldwide and had grossed more than US$200 million.

''Resident Evil'' is often cited as one of the [[List of video games considered the best|greatest and most influential video games ever made]]. It is credited with defining the survival horror genre and with returning zombies to [[popular culture]], leading to a renewed interest in [[zombie film]]s by the 2000s. It created [[Resident Evil|a franchise]] including video games, films, comics, novels, and other merchandise. It has been [[Porting# Porting of video games|ported]] to [[Sega Saturn]], [[Windows]] and [[Nintendo DS]]. Its sequel, ''[[Resident Evil 2]]'' was released in 1998. Both the game's [[Resident Evil (2002 video game)|remake]] and [[Resident Evil Zero|prequel]] were released on [[GameCube]] in 2002.

