'''''Resident Evil 2'''''{{efn|{{nihongo|Known in Japan as '''''Biohazard 2'''''|バイオハザード2|Baiohazādo Tsū|lead=yes}}}} is a 1998 [[survival horror]] game developed and published by [[Capcom]] for the [[PlayStation (console)|PlayStation]]. The player controls rookie cop [[Leon S. Kennedy]] and college student [[Claire Redfield]], who must escape Raccoon City after its citizens are transformed into [[Zombie (fictional)|zombies]] by a [[biological weapon]] two months after the events of the original ''[[Resident Evil (1996 video game)|Resident Evil]]''. The gameplay focuses on exploration, puzzles, and combat; the main difference from its predecessor are the branching paths, with each [[player character]] having unique storylines, partners and obstacles.

''Resident Evil 2'' was produced by ''Resident Evil'' director [[Shinji Mikami]], directed by [[Hideki Kamiya]], and developed by a team of approximately 50 across 21 months. The initial version, commonly referred to as ''[[Resident Evil 1.5]]'', differs drastically; it was canceled at approximately two thirds completion because Mikami decided it was inadequate. The final design introduced a more cinematic presentation.

''Resident Evil 2'' received acclaim for its atmosphere, setting, graphics, audio, scenarios, overall gameplay, and its improvements over the original game, but with some criticism towards its controls, voice acting, and certain gameplay elements. It is widely listed among the [[List of video games considered the best|best video games ever made]]. It is the best-selling ''[[Resident Evil]]'' game for a single platform at more than {{nowrap|6 million}} copies sold across all platforms. It was [[Port (video gaming)|ported]] to [[Windows]], [[Nintendo 64]], [[Dreamcast]], and [[GameCube]], and a modified [[2.5D]] version was released for the [[Game.com]] handheld. The story of ''Resident Evil 2'' was retold and built upon in several later games, and has been adapted into a variety of licensed works. It was followed by ''[[Resident Evil 3: Nemesis]]'' in 1999. A [[Resident Evil 2 (2019 video game)|remake]] was released for [[PlayStation 4]], Windows, and [[Xbox One]] in 2019.

