'''''Dragon Quest VIII: Journey of the Cursed King'''''{{efn|Known in Japan as {{nihongo|'''''Dragon Quest VIII: Sora to Umi to Daichi to Norowareshi Himegimi''''', {{lit}} "Dragon Quest VIII: Sky, Sea, Earth, and the Cursed Princess"|ドラゴンクエストVIII 空と海と大地と呪われし姫君|lead=yes}},<!-- See [[WP:JFN]] --> and in Australia and Europe as '''''Dragon Quest: The Journey of the Cursed King'''''.}} is a 2004 [[role-playing video game]] developed by [[Level-5 (company)|Level-5]] and published by [[Square Enix]] for the [[PlayStation 2]]. It was first released in Japan in November 2004, followed by North America in November 2005 and [[PAL region]]s in April 2006.<ref name=jenkins>{{cite web | author=Jenkins, David | date=April 23, 2009 | title=Square Enix Releases Tomb Raider, Dragon Quest Sales Data | url=http://gamasutra.com/php-bin/news_index.php?story=23329 | website=Gamasutra | access-date=April 23, 2009 | archive-date=August 12, 2017 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170812215106/http://gamasutra.com/php-bin/news_index.php?story=23329 | url-status=dead }}</ref> It is the eighth installment of the ''[[Dragon Quest]]'' series and it is the first English version of a ''Dragon Quest'' game to drop the ''Dragon Warrior'' title.<ref name="horii">{{cite web | author=Onyett, Charles | date=May 19, 2005 | title=E3 2005: Interview with Yuji Horii | url=http://www.ign.com/articles/2005/05/20/e3-2005-interview-with-yuji-horii | website=IGN | access-date=June 1, 2009 | archive-date=November 29, 2020 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201129061010/https://www.ign.com/articles/2005/05/20/e3-2005-interview-with-yuji-horii | url-status=live }}</ref> A version of the game for [[Android (operating system)|Android]] and [[iOS]] was released in Japan in 2013<ref name="dq1-8-mobile"/> and worldwide in 2014,<ref name="itunes_release" /><ref name="google_play_release" /> with a version for [[Nintendo 3DS]] releasing later in 2015 in Japan and 2017 globally.

''Dragon Quest VIII'' uses [[cel shading]] for the characters and scenery and is the first game in the series to have fully [[3D computer graphics|3D]] environments and character models.<ref name="rank">{{cite web | year=2007 | title=Dragon Quest VIII at GameRankings.com | url=http://www.gamerankings.com/ps2/583527-dragon-quest-viii-journey-of-the-cursed-king/index.html | access-date=October 13, 2007 | archive-date=August 26, 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180826035412/http://www.gamerankings.com/ps2/583527-dragon-quest-viii-journey-of-the-cursed-king/index.html | url-status=live }}</ref> The game retains most of the series' role-playing game elements, such as turn-based combat and the experience level system. ''Dragon Quest VIII'' follows the silent protagonist and his party of allies as they journey towards the goal of defeating the wicked Dhoulmagus, who cursed the kingdom of Trodain and its people. ''Dragon Quest VIII'' was a critical and commercial success, and has appeared on various [[List of video games listed among the best|best-of video game lists]].

