{{Nihongo foot|'''''Kirby and the Forgotten Land'''''|星のカービィ　ディスカバリー|Hoshi no Kābī Disukabarī|lit. "Kirby of the Stars: Discovery"|lead=yes|group=lower-alpha}} is a 2022 [[Platformer|platform game]] developed by [[HAL Laboratory]] and published by [[Nintendo]] for the [[Nintendo Switch]]. Released on March 25, 2022, is the thirteenth mainline installment in the [[Kirby (series)|''Kirby'' series]] and the second on the Switch, as well as the first non-[[spinoff (media)|spinoff]] game in the series to be in full 3D. The player controls [[Kirby (character)|Kirby]] in an adventure through the titular forgotten land to rescue [[Waddle Dee]]s kidnapped by the ferocious Beast Pack. To complete each stage and save the Waddle Dees, Kirby can use a wide range of copy abilities to help battle enemies and progress the level.

''Kirby and the Forgotten Land'' was well received by critics, who praised its graphics, level design, gameplay, soundtrack, and amount of content, with some calling it among the best games in the series. Minor criticism was directed towards the limited movement options and controls and repetitive mini-bosses. The game was a commercial success, selling over 7.52 million copies by March 2024, making it the [[Kirby (series)#Sales|best-selling game in the series]] and one of the [[List of best-selling Nintendo Switch video games|best-selling games on the Switch]].

A Nintendo Switch 2 Edition of ''Kirby and the Forgotten Land'', an enhanced version of the game featuring improved performance and a new story campaign titled {{nihongo foot|'''''Star-Crossed World''''',|スターリーワールド|Sutārī Wārudo|lit. "Starry World"|lead=yes|group=lower-alpha}} was released for the [[Nintendo Switch 2]] on August 28, 2025. The next 3D game in the series, ''[[Kirby and the World Beyond]]'', is scheduled for release on the Switch 2 in Spring 2027.

